{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7886","id":5216972893,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNvSwXQ","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7886","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7886.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7886.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7886","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7886/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7886/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7886/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/8261c08041b784a76a8469ab48cf73b62db579fa","number":7886,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(deploy): slice 3 — real systemd activation with health-check flip-back (#5766)","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes the remaining acceptance of #5766 (deploy tool v1): slices 1–2 (PR #6231, PR #7692) shipped the registry, unit rendering, dry-run plans, generation log, and status/rollback logic; the non-dry-run paths refused explicitly. This slice implements real activation.\n\n**What changed**\n- `pkgs/deploy/deploy.py`: real (non-dry-run) `deploy` and `rollback` for the systemd class, in the design §4.1 plan order — install the generation into the per-service profile, write the unit, daemon-reload, restart only that unit, run the health check, flip back on any failure.\n  - The profile is deploy-managed: the profile link points at a generation directory whose `current` symlink names the artifact (the rendered unit's `<profile>/current/<entryPoint>` path resolves through it), so a flip is one atomic symlink repoint. Store-path artifacts are additionally registered with `nix-env --set` on a parallel `<name>.nix-env-profile`.\n  - Rollback repoints at the previous distinct generation and restarts — never a rebuild (§4.6). On health failure it flips back to the generation that was current.\n  - Failed activations append a non-folding `deploy_failed`/`rollback_failed` generation-log entry, so the current/previous fold never mistakes a failure for an activation.\n  - New `--unit-dir` / `--scope system|user` (user scope exists so the laptop E2E can deploy a harmless service without root). Launchd real activation still refuses explicitly — it cannot be exercised from the Linux fleet.\n- Tests: `test_deploy_slice3.py` (new, 7 tests, faked runner/prober asserting the §4.1 order, flip-back, rollback, and the recorded-not-raised flip-back-failure regression), wired into `lib/default.nix` checks as `deploy-slice3-tests`; the slice-2 refusal test updated to the new behavior. Slice-2 suite 21/21, slice-3 7/7, dupkeys/argv suites pass on the laptop.\n\n**Laptop E2E acceptance (2026-11-09T00:49Z, user scope, harmless `deploy-e2e` service, no nixos-rebuild / home-manager in the loop)** — full log on #5766 (comment 6729616258):\n1. deploy v1 → generation 1 activated, serves; status current gen 1, health ok.\n2. deploy v2 → generation 2, serves v2.\n3. rollback → serves v1 again.\n4. deploy broken generation → health check fails, auto-flips back to generation 3, serves v2, final status health ok.\n\nThe first E2E run caught a real bug — a broken unit restart-loops into systemd's start limit, so flip-back now issues `reset-failed` before restarting and never raises (a flip-back failure is a recorded outcome, not a crash).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796777463&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7886&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7886&signature=e951e3f98e9554247d291b5202fa8b4078d717b329300bb94f4834f6dddc93a7\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7886?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T00:50:54Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T10:20:33Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T10